; Interprets: RFC 6733
;; What RFC 6733's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. The base protocol's AVPs are read by every application, so
;; a block with no scope says only what the RFC says of the AVP wherever it
;; is sent; what it says of a message is read on its own commands, CER/CEA,
;; DWR/DWA, DPR/DPA, RAR/RAA, STR/STA, ASR/ASA and ACR/ACA, which no
;; application's own print of a command shares (docs/constraints.md,
;; Precedence). The header's fields and flags (sections 3 and 7.2: the
;; version, the R, P, E and T bits, a protocol error's E bit) are the
;; Wireshark plugin's checks of the header, and no block reads them. An
;; answer with the E bit set conforms to section 7.2's <answer-message> and
;; not to its command's CCF, so a rule on such an answer is `text-only`. A
;; rule depending on the node, the transport, the session or an earlier
;; message is `text-only` too.


;; Section 5.3.1 and 5.3.2: the transport is no part of the message.


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cer-host-ip-address-per-address
; AVP: Host-IP-Address
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 5.3.1
"When Diameter is run over SCTP [RFC4960] or DTLS/SCTP [RFC6083], which allow for connections to span multiple interfaces and multiple IP addresses, the Capabilities-Exchange-Request message MUST contain one Host-IP-Address AVP for each potential IP address that MAY be locally used when transmitting Diameter messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cea-host-ip-address-per-address
; AVP: Host-IP-Address
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Answer
; Section: 5.3.2
"When Diameter is run over SCTP [RFC4960] or DTLS/SCTP [RFC6083], which allow connections to span multiple interfaces, hence, multiple IP addresses, the Capabilities-Exchange-Answer message MUST contain one Host-IP-Address AVP for each potential IP address that MAY be locally used when transmitting Diameter messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: supported-vendor-id-not-zero
; AVP: Supported-Vendor-Id
; Section: 5.3.6
"The value of this AVP MUST NOT be set to zero."
    exclude 0


;; Section 6.1: CER, DPR and DWR, whose headers print no PXY, are the base
;; protocol's requests that cannot be proxied; their bodies admit the two
;; AVPs only through * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cer-destination-realm-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cer-destination-host-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dpr-destination-realm-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Disconnect-Peer-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dpr-destination-host-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Disconnect-Peer-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dwr-destination-realm-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Device-Watchdog-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dwr-destination-host-not-proxiable
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Device-Watchdog-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


;; Section 6.2: what an answer carries of its request's. Each request
;; prints the Session-Id its answer prints, and a relay or proxy passes
;; the answer on as received, its own Proxy-Info aside (section 6.2.2),
;; so the pair on each link is held to it; the ACA's Session-Id is read in
;; clause 9.7.2. CEA's, DPA's and DWA's requests carry no Session-Id and
;; no Proxy-Info (table 10.1).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: raa-session-id-the-requests
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"If the Session-Id is present in the request, it MUST be included in the answer."
    equals request/Session-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: asa-session-id-the-requests
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Abort-Session-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"If the Session-Id is present in the request, it MUST be included in the answer."
    equals request/Session-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-session-id-the-requests
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Session-Termination-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"If the Session-Id is present in the request, it MUST be included in the answer."
    equals request/Session-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: raa-proxy-info-the-requests
; AVP: Proxy-Info
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"Any Proxy-Info AVPs in the request MUST be added to the answer message, in the same order they were present in the request."
    present-if request/Proxy-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: asa-proxy-info-the-requests
; AVP: Proxy-Info
; Command: Abort-Session-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"Any Proxy-Info AVPs in the request MUST be added to the answer message, in the same order they were present in the request."
    present-if request/Proxy-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sta-proxy-info-the-requests
; AVP: Proxy-Info
; Command: Session-Termination-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"Any Proxy-Info AVPs in the request MUST be added to the answer message, in the same order they were present in the request."
    present-if request/Proxy-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-proxy-info-the-requests
; AVP: Proxy-Info
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 6.2
"Any Proxy-Info AVPs in the request MUST be added to the answer message, in the same order they were present in the request."
    present-if request/Proxy-Info


;; Whether a request is an unsolicited agent-initiated one is the node's;
;; the answers are read below, in each of the base protocol's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: destination-host-agent-initiated
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Section: 6.5
"This AVP MUST be present in all unsolicited agent initiated messages, MAY be present in request messages, and MUST NOT be present in answer messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cea-destination-host-absent
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Answer
; Section: 6.5
"This AVP MUST be present in all unsolicited agent initiated messages, MAY be present in request messages, and MUST NOT be present in answer messages."
    absent


